       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the analgesic benefit doesn't increase.\n\nThese are options within labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **400 mg PO, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day). These suit analgesia or lower-intensity needs.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg *per day*, for example 400 mg four times daily, I can enter that. If the goal is stronger pain control, I can help with a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a safe dose.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
